              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Gen. Mark J. Bennett, the 1993 congressional Apology Resolution was intended as a symbolic apology and did not alter Hawaii's right to transfer its public lands or repeal prior congressional enactments that extinguish competing claims."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Kannon K. Shanmugam",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7b71e5e2d8beed064dde295e1418f6a4a12534de208094bed020f7c713ac85a2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7b71e5e2d8be-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Kannon K. Shanmugam, the central legal question is whether the Apology Resolution created an affirmative federal obligation not to sell ceded Hawaiian lands."
      }
    ],
